---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Colour Transfer & Automated Colour Grading - François Pitié" currentSection="research">
  <div class="mb-8 pb-3 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC] mb-1">
      <a href="/research" class="hover:underline">&larr; Back to Research & Projects</a>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
      Colour Transfer & Automated Colour Grading
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">
      Mathematical formulations for probability density transfer and continuous Monge-Kantorovich optimal transport.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Hero Visual -->
  <div class="mb-8 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs">
    <img 
      src="/images/colourtransfer.jpg" 
      alt="Colour Transfer: Original, Target Palette, and After Transfer" 
      class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
    />
    <div class="p-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50">
      <strong>Figure: </strong> Example of colour transfer — (left) original image, (centre) target colour palette image, (right) resulting image after continuous distribution transfer.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-10">
    <p>
      <strong>Colour Transfer</strong> is the process of matching colour characteristics and colorimetric moods between different photographic images or video sequences. The fundamental challenge is determining a bijective transformation in 3D colour space that aligns the joint probability density function (PDF) of a source image with that of a reference grade without introducing contouring or gamut artefacts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our research introduced an exact, iterative solution to multi-dimensional probability density function transfer based on 1D Radon projections, alongside closed-form linear Monge-Kantorovich formulations. These mathematical frameworks became the technological foundation for commercial grading tools, notably <em>MatchGrade</em> in The Foundry's <strong>Furnace</strong> suite for Nuke.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Open Source Code & Resources -->
  <section class="mb-10 p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-200/60 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-700/80">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC]" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.484 2 12.017c0 4.425 2.865 8.18 6.839 9.504.5.092.682-.217.682-.483 0-.237-.008-.868-.013-1.703-2.782.605-3.369-1.343-3.369-1.343-.454-1.158-1.11-1.466-1.11-1.466-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.53 1.032 1.53 1.032.892 1.53 2.341 1.088 2.91.832.092-.647.35-1.088.636-1.338-2.22-.253-4.555-1.113-4.555-4.951 0-1.093.39-1.988 1.029-2.688-.103-.253-.446-1.272.098-2.65 0 0 .84-.27 2.75 1.026A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.296 2.747-1.027 2.747-1.027.546 1.379.202 2.398.1 2.651.64.7 1.028 1.595 1.028 2.688 0 3.848-2.339 4.695-4.566 4.943.359.309.678.92.678 1.855 0 1.338-.012 2.419-.012 2.747 0 .268.18.58.688.482A10.019 10.019 0 0022 12.017C22 6.484 17.522 2 12 2z"/>
      </svg>
      Reference Implementation & Code
    </h2>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">
      Reference MATLAB code implementing the iterative N-dimensional PDF transfer algorithm, the linear Monge-Kantorovich mapping, and post-filtering regraining routines.
    </p>
    <a 
      href="https://github.com/frcs/colour-transfer" 
      target="_blank" 
      rel="noopener noreferrer" 
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-[#0569B9] dark:text-[#82B4DC] hover:underline"
    >
      frcs/colour-transfer on GitHub &rarr;
    </a>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Publications -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white pb-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      Key Publications
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-l-2 border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pl-3.5 py-0.5 hover:border-[#0569B9] transition-colors">
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          Automated colour grading using colour distribution transfer
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">
          F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">
          <em>Computer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU)</em>, 107(1-2):123–137, 2007.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pl-3.5 py-0.5 hover:border-[#0569B9] transition-colors">
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          The linear Monge-Kantorovitch linear colour mapping for example-based colour transfer
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">
          F. Pitié and A. Kokaram
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">
          <em>4th European Conference on Visual Media Production (CVMP)</em>, London, 2007.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pl-3.5 py-0.5 hover:border-[#0569B9] transition-colors">
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          N-Dimensional Probability Density Function Transfer and its Application to Colour Transfer
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">
          F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">
          <em>Tenth IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)</em>, Beijing, 2005.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
